259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (After weeks of rigorous testing, we eventually decided that the obstruction of going up the ramp caused by the Omnidirectional X-Drive is too severe to be acceptable, while the cost of maintaining the rubber bands of the Central Omni Wheel system is also too large. In addition, as tests of the superstructure were done on the tank drive, it turned out that the robot could also complete tasks efficiently without the ability to move sideways. Thus, we decided to use the traditional tank drive with a 15:1 transmission ratio. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Nevertheless, there was a serious problem regarding the loosening of the shaft of the center wheel due to the loosening of the set screws on the motor. To solve this problem, we added one more motor frame to make room for a shaft clip to be added between the C-channel and the motor. Another shaft clip was placed outside the wheel, making the shaft more stable. Moreover, a notch was created for easier fastening of the set screws.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
