275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 627 0 R
/ActualText (The first iteration of our lift contained two 3-stage slides with a string-driven elevator mechanism. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 628 0 R
/ActualText (Even though this version successfully enabled us to score four balls at once, the maximum height was not high enough for scoring stably.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 155 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Resource Storage)
/E (Resource Storage)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 629 0 R
/ActualText (The first iteration of the storage bucket was placed at an incline, which caused interference with the sliding mechanism.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 630 0 R
/ActualText (The gears we used to pivot the ball storage at the top was also inconsistent. When we attempted to release the balls, the motor had to create a great deal of torque to tip the storage, which was too much for the plastic gear to withstand causing it to skip gears. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 631 0 R
/ActualText (A single gate was used to release the balls, but it only allowed the robot to release all four balls at once. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 632 0 R
/ActualText (Two aluminum extrusions were used to guide the balls; however, they could not prevent the balls from rubbing with each other, causing friction.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 633 0 R
/ActualText (Expandable panels were installed on the sides that increased the storage capacity of the robot. They could also be folded onto the top to ensure the robot did not exceed size limitations. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Iteration 2:)
/E (Iteration 2:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Lift)
/E (Lift)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Resource Storage)
/E (Resource Storage)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 634 0 R
/ActualText (For the second iteration, we changed the slide into a 4-stage continuous slide that was also driven by strings. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 635 0 R
/ActualText (After more rigorous testing, we discovered that the weight of the balls and the upper structure caused the elevator and upper structure to twist and shake as the robot moved and turned. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 636 0 R
/ActualText (In the second version, we changed our pivoting mechanism to use a chain, with the motors propelling the chain drive below the storage, so that we can use shorter electrical wires for the motor, while providing more stability for the spinning mechanism. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 637 0 R
/ActualText (The side panels were redesigned to more sufficiently fold to the sides.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 155 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
