328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 650 0 R
/ActualText (After we developed our second successful superstructure \(the four-slider system\), we found out that it is very likely that a team fails to release Energy and Water balls precisely and cause them to fall to the ground. Therefore, we decided to develop an intake system that can carry released Food balls as well as misplaced Water/Energy balls to the human player. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (11)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Iteration 1:)
/E (Iteration 1:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 651 0 R
/ActualText (The first version of the intake system consisted of two arms that are attached to the sides of the robot that could rotate up or down based on an axis. Their movement was restricted by two physical limits. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 652 0 R
/ActualText (The arms were held by rubber tubing in the back to ensure that it did not exceed size limitations when the robot was in its initial position. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 653 0 R
/ActualText (A motor was installed at the front of each arm that was attached to two intake flaps. When the flaps spun, balls could be taken in.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 158 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Iteration 2:)
/E (Iteration 2:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 158 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 654 0 R
/ActualText (The second version was largely similar to the first. We noticed that the intake flaps of the first version did not provide enough friction, so we switched the spinning mechanism to use a traction wheel instead.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 655 0 R
/ActualText (However, even though the friction of the traction wheels was sufficient, they would cause the arms to bend, which also led to the failure of the intake system. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 158 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
